Canadian Prairies QSO Party -- entries used by a station in Alberta, Saskatchewan or Manitoba
The 65 districts, each counting as its province, then DC as Maryland, the 50 states and the other 10 provinces and territories.
The district file comes FIRST, so a district code wins over any state alias spelled the same.
DC is mapped to Md before s50.dom: the sponsor chart says DC counts as MD.
The provinces are written here and P12/P13 are not included: their call-area aliases (VE1 to VY2) would let the rover strip take
a call such as W1AW/VE6, and AB, SK and MB are not received exchanges here (a prairie station sends its district), so those three
carry a display name only. NF and LB are read as NL.
No line of this header may hold an equals sign: the reader takes any such line as an entry.

INCLUDE FILE cpqp_cty.dom
Dc > Md = DC
INCLUDE FILE s50.dom
Bc = BC,^British Columbia
On = ON,^Ontario
Qc = QC,^Quebec
Nb = NB,^New Brunswick
Ns = NS,^Nova Scotia
Pe = PE,^Prince Edward Island
Nl = NL,NF,LB,^Newfoundland and Labrador
Nt = NT,^Northwest Territories
Nu = NU,^Nunavut
Yt = YT,^Yukon
Ab = ^Alberta
Sk = ^Saskatchewan
Mb = ^Manitoba
